<section class="ho-faq" id="faq">
  <div class="ho-faq__inner">
    <div class="ho-faq__header fade-in">
      <span class="ho-eyebrow">Questions</span>
      <h2 class="ho-faq__title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <p>Honest answers about Huper Optik window film in Philadelphia from specialists with over 16 years of installation experience.</p>
      <a href="/contact/" class="ho-faq__cta-btn">Talk to a Specialist</a>
    </div>
    <div class="ho-faq__list fade-in">
      <div class="ho-faq__item ho-faq__item--open">
        <div class="ho-faq__q"><span>What is Huper Optik window film in Philadelphia and what makes it different from standard film?</span><span class="ho-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="ho-faq__a"><p>Huper Optik uses a patented dual-layer Titanium Nitride (TiN) ceramic coating — 100% metal-free construction that rejects infrared heat and UV rays without affecting wireless signals or GPS.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="ho-faq__item">
        <div class="ho-faq__q"><span>What is Titanium Nitride (TiN) ceramic coating and why does it matter for Philadelphia buildings?</span><span class="ho-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="ho-faq__a"><p>TiN is a ceramic compound applied in dual layers to the film substrate. The construction earned a US patent and delivers high IR rejection without metallic materials that could interfere with Wi-Fi, GPS, or cellular signals.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="ho-faq__item">
        <div class="ho-faq__q"><span>Will Huper Optik Ceramic film interfere with Wi-Fi, GPS, or cellular signals in my Philadelphia office?</span><span class="ho-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="ho-faq__a"><p>No. The 100% metal-free ceramic construction does not affect any wireless signals, cellular coverage, GPS performance, or electronic key fobs.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="ho-faq__item">
        <div class="ho-faq__q"><span>Which Huper Optik series is best for Philadelphia rowhomes with older single-pane glass?</span><span class="ho-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="ho-faq__a"><p>Therm-X is the best fit for older single-pane glass — its low-emissivity construction improves year-round thermal performance in both summer and winter without replacing the window.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="ho-faq__item">
        <div class="ho-faq__q"><span>How does Huper Optik Therm-X help with Philadelphia's winters as well as summers?</span><span class="ho-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="ho-faq__a"><p>Therm-X adds a low-emissivity layer that helps retain interior heat in winter while still rejecting solar gain in summer — ideal for Philadelphia's Zone 4A mixed-humid climate.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="ho-faq__item">
        <div class="ho-faq__q"><span>What VLT options does the Huper Optik Ceramic Series offer for Philadelphia commercial projects?</span><span class="ho-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="ho-faq__a"><p>The Ceramic Series ranges from C5 (6% VLT) to C85 (85% VLT) across 11 options — covering everything from near-blackout privacy to nearly clear glass for daylighting-focused commercial projects.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="ho-faq__item">
        <div class="ho-faq__q"><span>Can Huper Optik window film be specified for LEED projects in Philadelphia?</span><span class="ho-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="ho-faq__a"><p>Yes. Huper Optik solar control film data can support LEED energy and atmosphere documentation when the project requirements and modeled performance align with the applicable credit criteria.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="ho-faq__item">
        <div class="ho-faq__q"><span>How does Huper Optik Ceramic compare to 3M Prestige or LLumar ATC for Philadelphia offices?</span><span class="ho-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="ho-faq__a"><p>Huper Optik Ceramic delivers comparable UV block (99%) with the added advantage of 100% metal-free construction. For signal-sensitive Philadelphia office buildings, the TiN ceramic construction is a meaningful specification differentiator.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="ho-faq__item">
        <div class="ho-faq__q"><span>What warranty does Huper Optik offer for commercial window film in Philadelphia?</span><span class="ho-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="ho-faq__a"><p>Solar control and insulating series carry lifetime residential and 15-year commercial warranty coverage. Shield safety film carries 10-year commercial coverage. Decorative series have 7-year coverage.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="ho-faq__item">
        <div class="ho-faq__q"><span>Which Philadelphia neighborhoods and building types see the most Huper Optik installations?</span><span class="ho-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="ho-faq__a"><p>Huper Optik is common in Center City commercial offices, Chestnut Hill and Fishtown rowhomes, Rittenhouse restaurant and retail glass, University City institutional buildings, and Old City historic properties.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

